/-!
# The XOR cipher on an array

The Rust function combines every byte of an array with a key by exclusive or,
the cipher of `XorCipher.lean` of the morning session:

```rust
pub fn xor_encrypt<const N: usize>(mut data: [u8; N], key: u8) -> [u8; N] {
    let mut i: usize = 0;
    while i < N {
        data[i] = data[i] ^ key;
        i += 1;
    }
    data
}
```

Unlike `max_element`, this loop modifies the array.

This cipher is a toy: with a key of one byte, it is broken by trying all 256
keys. What is verified below is that the function computes what it should, not
that the encryption is secure.

## The generated definitions

The loop is translated as in `MaxArray_verified.lean`, with the state
`(data, i)`. The assignment `data[i] = …` becomes `Array.update data i i2`,
which returns a new array equal to `data` except at position `i`, and which
fails when `i` is outside the array. Exclusive or on bytes cannot fail; the
library function `lift`, with `lift x = ok x`, turns its value into a `Result`.
The function `xor_encrypt` only calls the loop, and it carries the attribute
`@[reducible]`, so that tactics such as `step` see through it to the call of
`xor_encrypt_loop`.
-/

namespace xor_cipher

/-- [xor_cipher::xor_encrypt]: loop body 0:
    Source: 'xor_cipher/src/lib.rs', lines 3:4-6:5
    Visibility: public -/
@[rust_loop_body]
def xor_encrypt_loop.body
  {N : Std.Usize} (key : Std.U8) (data : Array Std.U8 N) (i : Std.Usize) :
  Result (ControlFlow ((Array Std.U8 N) × Std.Usize) (Array Std.U8 N))
  := do
  if i < N
  then
    let i1 ← Array.index_usize data i
    let i2 ← lift (i1 ^^^ key)
    let a ← Array.update data i i2
    let i3 ← i + 1#usize
    ok (cont (a, i3))
  else ok (done data)

/-- [xor_cipher::xor_encrypt]: loop 0:
    Source: 'xor_cipher/src/lib.rs', lines 3:4-6:5
    Visibility: public -/
@[rust_loop]
def xor_encrypt_loop
  {N : Std.Usize} (data : Array Std.U8 N) (key : Std.U8) (i : Std.Usize) :
  Result (Array Std.U8 N)
  := do
  loop
    (fun (data1, i1) => xor_encrypt_loop.body key data1 i1)
    (data, i)

/-- [xor_cipher::xor_encrypt]:
    Source: 'xor_cipher/src/lib.rs', lines 1:0-8:1
    Visibility: public -/
@[reducible]
def xor_encrypt
  {N : Std.Usize} (data : Array Std.U8 N) (key : Std.U8) :
  Result (Array Std.U8 N)
  := do
  xor_encrypt_loop data key 0#usize


